Maintenance of Power Circuit Breakers — FIST 3-16 (@pe-fist-breakers: 0, is #reference, #part-of @pe-sources) { r_6YDRQ4GKWPW34WTZ4AVJZHGKP4
U.S. Bureau of Reclamation, Power Resources Office and Technical Service Center. Maintenance of Power Circuit Breakers, FIST 3-16, May 2024. [Complete 99-file-page manual](https://www.usbr.gov/power/data/fist/FIST_3-16_%285-2024%29.pdf) · [Official catalogue](https://www.usbr.gov/power/data/fist_pub.html).

Read the whole manual and the complete applicable equipment-type sections. Relate interruption ratings and mechanisms to contact resistance, timing/motion, controls, insulation, inspection, condition evidence and maintenance decisions. Use actual manufacturer instructions and current operating requirements for the chosen breaker.

Title, contents and revision notice were inspected on 29 October 2026: the underlying release is June 2020, with minor revisions approved 29 May 2024. The catalogue states that 4-1B supersedes equipment-specific schedules. The document is written for Reclamation's staff and equipment; its particular voltage categories and practices are not universal definitions. Public access does not remove separately credited component rights. No manual, test records or product data are bundled.

**Return:** [Power-engineering sources — complete books, courses, methods and evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_12EFX00X7ZXGT9MPMJDYRTNY9N).
